1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,137
Infections from a new virus are spreading.

2
00:00:04,204 --> 00:00:06,306
<i>There is a possibility</i>

3
00:00:06,373 --> 00:00:09,409
<i>that one person has been infected</i>
<i>at this hospital!</i>

4
00:00:09,476 --> 00:00:11,978
I am proclaiming a state of emergency!

5
00:00:12,545 --> 00:00:14,247
<i>Code CBR!</i>

6
00:00:14,314 --> 00:00:17,083
<i>I repeat, code CBR!</i>

7
00:00:17,717 --> 00:00:19,686
<i>Code CBR!</i>

8
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:21,321
Code CBR?

9
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:22,489
This is really bad!

10
00:00:22,555 --> 00:00:24,157
What about the opening ceremony?

11
00:00:24,224 --> 00:00:26,092
There's no time for that! Let's go!

12
00:00:26,159 --> 00:00:27,193
<i>Code CBR!</i>

13
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,595
<i>Code CBR!</i>

14
00:00:29,162 --> 00:00:31,998
<i>The Infection Research Center</i>
<i>is off limits!</i>

15
00:00:32,065 --> 00:00:33,900
<i>Evacuate immediately!</i>

16
00:00:35,435 --> 00:00:36,970
<i>2021.</i>

17
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:40,440
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

18
00:00:40,507 --> 00:00:42,609
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

19
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:47,580
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

20
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:50,617
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

21
00:00:51,785 --> 00:00:52,786
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

22
00:00:52,852 --> 00:00:55,388
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

23
00:00:55,955 --> 00:00:59,859
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

24
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,962
Dr. Daimon, what are you doing?

25
00:01:03,029 --> 00:01:04,564
Get out now!

26
00:01:05,331 --> 00:01:06,966
Dr. Daimon!

27
00:01:08,968 --> 00:01:11,037
<i>She hates groups,</i>

28
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:14,274
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

29
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,942
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

30
00:01:16,509 --> 00:01:19,813
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

31
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:21,047
<i>to work her way up.</i>

32
00:01:21,614 --> 00:01:26,419
<i>Code CBR. The Infection Research</i>
<i>Center is off limits. Evacuate.</i>

33
00:01:26,486 --> 00:01:29,956
INFECTION RESEARCH CENTER
OPENING CEREMONY

34
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:34,394
Dr. Daimon…

35
00:01:36,729 --> 00:01:38,498
RYUTARO HACHISUKA, CHIEF OF
MEDICAL SOLUTIONS HEADQUARTERS

36
00:01:39,866 --> 00:01:41,267
<i>Dr. Michiko Daimon…</i>

37
00:01:41,801 --> 00:01:43,169
If possible,

38
00:01:44,471 --> 00:01:45,305
I want…

39
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:49,442
I want you to operate on me!

40
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:56,149
Wait!

41
00:01:56,216 --> 00:01:57,317
Don't close that!

42
00:02:11,097 --> 00:02:12,365
I've sworn I'll operate!

43
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:15,602
No sudden cancellations!

44
00:02:30,416 --> 00:02:32,552
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

45
00:02:33,553 --> 00:02:36,489
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

46
00:03:42,188 --> 00:03:43,823
<i>Do we need to run away?</i>

47
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:47,093
Chief Hachisuka has sealed off
the Infection Research Center

48
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,462
and has quarantined the infected person.

49
00:03:49,529 --> 00:03:50,363
I see.

50
00:03:51,097 --> 00:03:55,401
In that case, let's leave this
up to Dr. Hachisuka.

51
00:03:55,468 --> 00:03:56,402
Yes, sir.

52
00:03:57,337 --> 00:03:59,505
But is it okay to leave it all up to him?

53
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:02,108
The first infection happened
at our very own hospital!

54
00:04:02,675 --> 00:04:03,610
- Dr. Ebina.
- Yes?

55
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,845
I am a very busy man.

56
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:06,879
Yes, sir.

57
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,982
What's with all that "Yes, sir"?

58
00:04:09,048 --> 00:04:11,351
I thought you did this? And what's that?

59
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:14,120
Why are you wearing a trademark
yellow Hiruma necktie?

60
00:04:14,654 --> 00:04:16,122
Acting Director Hiruma

61
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:19,626
is at a key juncture
and is about to checkmate his opponent.

62
00:04:19,692 --> 00:04:20,994
Hold on here!

63
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:23,596
When did you play chess
with Acting Director Hiruma?

64
00:04:23,663 --> 00:04:25,098
- Dr. Ebina.
- Yes?

65
00:04:25,164 --> 00:04:28,001
People who are far from the seats of power

66
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:32,739
can't understand
this complex mental state I'm in.

67
00:04:33,339 --> 00:04:34,540
But=\\=

68
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,542
- Yes?
- Excuse me.

69
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:42,248
Acting Director Hiruma,
I made tea perfectly safe from infection.

70
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:45,251
You sure are thoughtful.

71
00:04:45,318 --> 00:04:46,152
Goodbye.

72
00:04:46,219 --> 00:04:47,353
Thank you.

73
00:04:49,022 --> 00:04:52,325
That thing we discussed, leave that to me.

74
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:56,963
Yes, sir.

75
00:04:57,597 --> 00:04:58,531
Good.

76
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,373
What's your problem?

77
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:08,641
You want to fight?

78
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:12,445
A new virus
that started in West Africa, huh?

79
00:05:12,512 --> 00:05:15,448
And it's already in Japan?
That sure is really fast!

80
00:05:16,249 --> 00:05:20,486
I know it's a little late for this,
but what is "Code CBR"?

81
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:27,593
It means "chemical, biological,
or radiological".

82
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,495
Thank you.

83
00:05:29,562 --> 00:05:30,663
What?

84
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:34,133
Rumor is this is several times
more infectious than COVID!

85
00:05:34,901 --> 00:05:37,570
The risk of severe illness is high too.

86
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,472
Deaths have increased lately.

87
00:05:39,539 --> 00:05:42,575
There's no treatment and who knows
if the vaccine is effective.

88
00:05:42,642 --> 00:05:45,678
It's much more virulent
and it can spread through the air!

89
00:05:45,745 --> 00:05:48,414
This says you can prevent it
by drinking boiling water!

90
00:05:48,481 --> 00:05:49,682
- What?
- Well…

91
00:05:49,749 --> 00:05:52,251
Viruses do die in boiling water.
Don't be stupid!

92
00:05:52,318 --> 00:05:54,687
Doctors shouldn't believe
everything on the Internet!

93
00:05:54,754 --> 00:05:56,289
But of all places,

94
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:58,524
we've got an infection
here at our hospital.

95
00:05:59,158 --> 00:06:01,260
If there's an outbreak here…

96
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:03,396
It will be a second pandemic!

97
00:06:03,896 --> 00:06:05,031
Calm down, would you?

98
00:06:05,631 --> 00:06:09,869
But we still don't have
a handle on COVID-19 yet.

99
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:13,573
We don't have a handle on MERS,
Ebola, or even AIDS!

100
00:06:13,639 --> 00:06:14,941
What are you so upset about?

101
00:06:27,453 --> 00:06:31,090
Well… Dr. Ebina, what will happen to us?

102
00:06:31,591 --> 00:06:32,959
I really do wonder.

103
00:06:36,662 --> 00:06:39,298
I'm going back to New York
before Japan is locked down.

104
00:06:39,365 --> 00:06:40,299
- Out of the way!
- Whoa!

105
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,735
He's running away again?

106
00:06:42,802 --> 00:06:43,970
He sure scrams fast.

107
00:06:44,704 --> 00:06:48,474
Has Chief Hachisuka shut himself
in the Infection Research Center?

108
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:53,646
Yes. He's treating the person
infected with the new virus.

109
00:06:53,713 --> 00:06:55,982
I guess the patient
brought it from abroad.

110
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,352
It's not clear,

111
00:06:59,419 --> 00:07:02,755
but Chief Hachisuka is developing
medication that is effective

112
00:07:02,822 --> 00:07:04,824
<i>against any kind of coronavirus.</i>

113
00:07:04,891 --> 00:07:07,393
I believe he'll administer it
to the patient.

114
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,128
I see.

115
00:07:09,195 --> 00:07:11,898
If the trial is a success,
it can be announced

116
00:07:11,964 --> 00:07:13,399
at medical conferences worldwide.

117
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:15,501
I can't believe you people.

118
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:18,604
You're only thinking about
your own status in this emergency.

119
00:07:18,671 --> 00:07:19,505
So?

120
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:21,541
Is that any way to react?

121
00:07:22,141 --> 00:07:23,543
Don't try to get ahead!

122
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:25,011
You're playing chess, right?

123
00:07:25,077 --> 00:07:28,548
Don't say such spiteful things
during an emergency.

124
00:07:29,215 --> 00:07:30,216
Unbelievable.

125
00:07:32,885 --> 00:07:33,886
Hey,

126
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:35,988
I'm operating tomorrow, so open the OR.

127
00:07:36,055 --> 00:07:36,889
Are you insane?

128
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:38,591
Otherwise, it will be too late.

129
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:40,359
It's a Code CBR, you know!

130
00:07:40,426 --> 00:07:42,495
Surgeries won't be possible
for quite a while.

131
00:07:42,562 --> 00:07:45,364
Locally advanced pancreatic cancer,
stage 3.

132
00:07:46,165 --> 00:07:48,401
A seven-centimeter tumor
on the pancreatic tail.

133
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:50,269
It has infiltrated several organs

134
00:07:50,336 --> 00:07:52,238
and is touching the ventral aorta.

135
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:53,439
It's growing fast.

136
00:07:53,506 --> 00:07:56,309
If we don't operate now,
his chances will go from 100 to zero.

137
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,579
Demon, what are you so worked up about?

138
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:00,613
Who's the patient?

139
00:08:01,347 --> 00:08:03,015
RYUTARO HACHISUKA

140
00:08:03,082 --> 00:08:04,417
"Ryutaro Hachisuka"?

141
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:06,018
- What?
- What?

142
00:08:06,085 --> 00:08:07,620
- Chief Hachisuka?
- Really?

143
00:08:08,454 --> 00:08:09,822
Dr. Daimon,

144
00:08:09,889 --> 00:08:12,158
you knew about his pancreatic cancer?

145
00:08:12,225 --> 00:08:13,726
What? You knew about it?

146
00:08:16,562 --> 00:08:18,164
This is bad.

147
00:08:18,231 --> 00:08:21,400
Even for you, Dr. Daimon,
this is nearly impossible!

148
00:08:21,467 --> 00:08:24,470
Even chemical surgery didn't work,
so this is pointless.

149
00:08:25,805 --> 00:08:28,541
Your chemical surgery failed.

150
00:08:28,608 --> 00:08:32,078
But through surgery, I will succeed 100%!

151
00:08:32,144 --> 00:08:33,946
That's 100% impossible!

152
00:08:34,013 --> 00:08:36,415
What's more, you can't operate
during a Code CBR.

153
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:39,185
Dr. Daimon,
are you trying to kill Dr. Hachisuka?

154
00:08:39,785 --> 00:08:42,288
Well, I guess some people
would like that though.

155
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,956
Stop butting in.

156
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:46,826
As the acting representative
of the Acting Director,

157
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:48,494
I won't allow surgery!

158
00:08:48,561 --> 00:08:49,962
What's an "acting representative"?

159
00:08:50,029 --> 00:08:50,930
I don't know.

160
00:08:52,164 --> 00:08:53,165
Oh, man.

161
00:08:53,232 --> 00:08:54,467
Fine.

162
00:08:56,102 --> 00:08:57,136
Even with this?

163
00:08:59,338 --> 00:09:00,673
SURGERY CONSENT FORM

164
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:01,574
RYUTARO HACHISUKA

165
00:09:01,641 --> 00:09:02,975
A surgery consent form?

166
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,962
<i>It will be harder than today's surgery.</i>

167
00:09:23,029 --> 00:09:23,863
<i>But…</i>

168
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:28,167
I'll make it 100% perfect
like you prefer, Dr. Hachisuka.

169
00:09:29,035 --> 00:09:31,771
<i>I will not fail.</i>

170
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:46,252
Hello?

171
00:09:46,819 --> 00:09:50,656
<i>- This is Dr. Hachisuka.</i>
- Oh, my! Dr. Hachisuka!

172
00:09:51,223 --> 00:09:52,858
How are you feeling?

173
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:54,527
Quite well.

174
00:09:55,127 --> 00:09:56,562
<i>I'm glad to hear it.</i>

175
00:09:57,363 --> 00:09:59,932
Dr. Daimon never makes mistakes,
after all.

176
00:10:03,569 --> 00:10:05,705
You must be a truly happy person.

177
00:10:06,906 --> 00:10:07,940
Yes, I am.

178
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,078
Dr. Hachisuka.

179
00:10:12,144 --> 00:10:13,779
<i>Is there something wrong?</i>

180
00:10:14,714 --> 00:10:15,548
No.

181
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,917
I'm glad that you are recuperating well,

182
00:10:18,517 --> 00:10:20,853
but there's a patient with the new virus.

183
00:10:21,721 --> 00:10:24,123
Please be very careful, Mrs. Hiruma.

184
00:10:25,191 --> 00:10:27,660
I won't be Mrs. Hiruma for much longer.

185
00:10:27,727 --> 00:10:29,795
When I'm released, I'm getting divorced.

186
00:10:31,430 --> 00:10:32,798
Is that so?

187
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:36,769
I am actually glad that I had cancer.

188
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:41,140
There are some things you don't realize
until you become ill.

189
00:10:47,046 --> 00:10:51,484
Please take the life
that Dr. Daimon saved…

190
00:10:53,352 --> 00:10:55,287
and treat it preciously.

191
00:10:55,855 --> 00:10:58,691
Thank you, Dr. Hachisuka.

192
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,395
- Dr. Daimon!
- Hello? Hacchi?

193
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:05,297
<i>Your turn is next.</i>

194
00:11:05,364 --> 00:11:07,199
I'll operate tomorrow as planned.

195
00:11:07,266 --> 00:11:08,200
<i>What?</i>

196
00:11:09,201 --> 00:11:10,202
Dr. Daimon,

197
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,805
I'm terribly sorry.

198
00:11:14,306 --> 00:11:17,843
But you don't need to operate anymore.

199
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:18,978
Are you insane?

200
00:11:19,478 --> 00:11:20,646
Goodbye.

201
00:11:20,713 --> 00:11:21,814
Hello? Wait!

202
00:11:28,621 --> 00:11:32,358
If we all have to start
staying at home again,

203
00:11:32,425 --> 00:11:36,662
I won't be able to have
delicious meat like this anymore.

204
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:37,997
Eat up too.

205
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:41,067
Oh, that's right! You're a vegetarian.

206
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:43,703
Sorry for ordering the same thing again.

207
00:11:43,769 --> 00:11:46,138
- It's okay. I will eat it.
- What?

208
00:11:53,479 --> 00:11:54,747
- Yes, sir!
- What?

209
00:11:55,281 --> 00:11:57,049
- It's delicious!
- Oh, good.

210
00:11:57,116 --> 00:11:57,983
Hey…

211
00:11:58,851 --> 00:12:01,921
How's the branch hospital
rebuilding plan going?

212
00:12:01,987 --> 00:12:03,823
Isn't the contract signing tomorrow?

213
00:12:03,889 --> 00:12:05,825
Don't worry.

214
00:12:09,829 --> 00:12:12,465
It is in the hands
of this consulting company.

215
00:12:12,531 --> 00:12:15,301
- I see!
- Leave this to us.

216
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:25,478
You won't regret this.

217
00:12:30,349 --> 00:12:31,951
- There, there.
- How cute!

218
00:12:32,017 --> 00:12:33,919
I read on the Internet that

219
00:12:33,986 --> 00:12:36,622
this new virus can be caught by cats.

220
00:12:36,689 --> 00:12:38,157
That's just a rumor.

221
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:40,760
Fear and dread spread so easily.

222
00:12:40,826 --> 00:12:42,428
They're scarier than the virus.

223
00:12:43,295 --> 00:12:44,196
I'm back.

224
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:46,232
- Welcome home, Michiko!
- Welcome home!

225
00:12:46,298 --> 00:12:48,334
- Don't move!
- Time to disinfect.

226
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,169
- Here we go.
- Here.

227
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:51,604
- Turn around.
- Okay.

228
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:55,207
COVID was finally settling down,

229
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:57,576
but now we're back
doing the same thing again.

230
00:12:57,643 --> 00:13:01,647
And we can't do surgeries,
so business will plummet again.

231
00:13:01,714 --> 00:13:04,216
I guess tomorrow's surgery is postponed.

232
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:05,351
No. I'm doing it.

233
00:13:05,417 --> 00:13:07,119
That pancreas surgery?

234
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:08,020
Yes.

235
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:09,955
Is this surgery that important?

236
00:13:10,022 --> 00:13:11,023
<i>News flash.</i>

237
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:15,060
<i>- Yesterday at Totei University…</i>
- See?

238
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:19,198
"Infected patient hospitalized
at Totei University Hospital

239
00:13:19,265 --> 00:13:20,866
under quarantine."

240
00:13:21,367 --> 00:13:23,469
This is no time for surgery.

241
00:13:23,536 --> 00:13:26,105
<i>We're speaking with Dr. Hachisuka</i>
<i>of Totei University's</i>

242
00:13:26,172 --> 00:13:27,907
<i>Infection Research Center.</i>

243
00:13:28,407 --> 00:13:29,542
<i>Good evening.</i>

244
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:30,643
<i>I'm Dr. Hachisuka.</i>

245
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:34,046
<i>You found the first case</i>
<i>of the new virus in Japan.</i>

246
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:36,448
<i>How is the patient's condition?</i>

247
00:13:36,949 --> 00:13:41,086
<i>They have a slight fever</i>
<i>and general fatigue.</i>

248
00:13:41,687 --> 00:13:46,358
I swear that this
Infection Research Center will prevent

249
00:13:46,425 --> 00:13:48,194
the nationwide spread of the virus.

250
00:13:48,761 --> 00:13:52,264
The fundamental measures
for any kind of virus are

251
00:13:52,965 --> 00:13:54,934
wearing a mask and hand washing.

252
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,305
Dr. Hachisuka has pancreatic cancer.

253
00:13:59,972 --> 00:14:01,807
What? Pancreatic cancer?

254
00:14:02,608 --> 00:14:04,577
Is Dr. Hachisuka really that sick?

255
00:14:06,312 --> 00:14:07,913
But for the patient's sake,

256
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:09,114
he's still battling

257
00:14:09,648 --> 00:14:12,051
this new virus in his condition.

258
00:14:12,618 --> 00:14:14,386
<i>The best measures are…</i>

259
00:14:14,987 --> 00:14:16,755
That infection maniac.

260
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:21,060
<i>Even if it is an unknown virus,</i>

261
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:25,431
<i>wearing a mask and washing your hands</i>
<i>will protect you.</i>

262
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:23,555
BODY TEMPERATURE

263
00:15:52,751 --> 00:15:55,154
- I'll be leaving soon.
- Thank you.

264
00:15:56,388 --> 00:15:59,358
Are you planning that surgery again?

265
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,528
I'll do it alone.

266
00:16:03,362 --> 00:16:04,797
Don't be silly, Ms. Daimon.

267
00:16:07,399 --> 00:16:09,335
I bet he's infected.

268
00:16:10,035 --> 00:16:12,805
You're not planning to operate
if he is, are you?

269
00:16:13,572 --> 00:16:14,873
Like that other time?

270
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:17,109
Ms. Daimon! Open up!

271
00:16:19,745 --> 00:16:21,213
- Demon!
- Dr. Daimon!

272
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,382
Dr. Daimon, hang in there!

273
00:16:23,449 --> 00:16:25,918
That Lassa fever really did you in!

274
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,753
You were hospitalized for two months!

275
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,089
Both Akira and I were seriously worried

276
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:31,957
that you would never operate again!

277
00:16:32,024 --> 00:16:34,693
Fine. I know!
I won't be so reckless again.

278
00:16:36,362 --> 00:16:37,696
Getting infected

279
00:16:37,763 --> 00:16:41,867
when you're an infectious diseases
specialist is inexcusable.

280
00:16:44,536 --> 00:16:48,240
He's focusing on his own work
without running from the virus.

281
00:16:48,907 --> 00:16:49,975
That's why…

282
00:16:51,076 --> 00:16:52,444
I will operate.

283
00:16:58,317 --> 00:16:59,418
Ms. Daimon.

284
00:17:02,254 --> 00:17:03,689
You like Hacchi, don't you?

285
00:17:04,556 --> 00:17:05,391
What?

286
00:17:06,258 --> 00:17:09,762
Listen. This is what
that infection maniac does, you know.

287
00:17:11,163 --> 00:17:13,198
Don't be stupid.

288
00:17:17,069 --> 00:17:18,170
I'm home.

289
00:17:18,771 --> 00:17:21,640
I ran into these guys
on the way back from the bath.

290
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:22,941
Come in.

291
00:17:23,008 --> 00:17:25,044
Good evening! Dr. Daimon! Good to see you!

292
00:17:25,644 --> 00:17:27,379
Sorry to drop by so late.

293
00:17:27,446 --> 00:17:28,814
You have one more cat!

294
00:17:29,415 --> 00:17:31,150
How cute!

295
00:17:32,251 --> 00:17:34,386
- What's its name?
- Shut up and leave!

296
00:17:34,453 --> 00:17:35,287
Demon!

297
00:17:35,888 --> 00:17:37,756
We have urgent business to discuss.

298
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:43,562
You sure look mad.

299
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:46,198
So,

300
00:17:46,799 --> 00:17:49,234
what is this urgent business?

301
00:17:49,301 --> 00:17:50,235
Dr. Daimon,

302
00:17:51,103 --> 00:17:54,373
we think we've got
Dr. Hachisuka all wrong.

303
00:17:56,075 --> 00:18:01,013
He's ignoring his own illness
to save the infected patient.

304
00:18:01,547 --> 00:18:03,449
He really is a fool.

305
00:18:04,149 --> 00:18:06,118
Cancer has weakened his immune system

306
00:18:06,185 --> 00:18:07,886
and raised the risk of infection.

307
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,589
He should know that very well.

308
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:14,760
He's more worried about patients
than his own status.

309
00:18:14,827 --> 00:18:16,228
He's a model physician!

310
00:18:18,063 --> 00:18:19,064
And?

311
00:18:22,634 --> 00:18:25,971
Will you let us help you
with Dr. Hachisuka's surgery?

312
00:18:26,638 --> 00:18:27,473
Please!

313
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,141
I'll help too.

314
00:18:29,208 --> 00:18:33,345
I'll stake my reputation
as former Head of Surgery

315
00:18:33,412 --> 00:18:34,446
on securing an OR.

316
00:18:34,513 --> 00:18:36,381
I won't let Dr. Kuwagata interfere.

317
00:18:37,015 --> 00:18:38,250
Even if you want to operate,

318
00:18:38,851 --> 00:18:40,185
hasn't Dr. Hachisuka shut himself

319
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:44,223
inside the Infection Research Center
with the patient?

320
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:47,059
He's inside and he won't open up, right?

321
00:18:47,693 --> 00:18:48,594
That's right.

322
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:51,263
We've developed a plan for luring him out.

323
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:54,333
A plan?

324
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:14,019
Chief Hachisuka, Dr. Ebina speaking.

325
00:19:14,086 --> 00:19:15,521
How is the patient doing?

326
00:19:15,587 --> 00:19:17,222
They're currently stable.

327
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,725
<i>You won't last in there alone.</i>

328
00:19:19,791 --> 00:19:21,960
I've brought help, so let us take over.

329
00:19:22,528 --> 00:19:26,064
An infectious disease novice
can't do this job. Please leave.

330
00:19:26,131 --> 00:19:28,200
<i>Hey! Dr. Hachisuka! Dr. Kaji here!</i>

331
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:30,369
<i>You sure are stubborn!</i>

332
00:19:30,435 --> 00:19:33,405
<i>Fine. We brought you food and water.</i>

333
00:19:33,472 --> 00:19:35,274
<i>And protective gear and masks.</i>

334
00:19:35,874 --> 00:19:37,409
<i>Do you need anything else?</i>

335
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,178
No, I'm fine.

336
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:41,713
At least open up down here.

337
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:44,850
<i>Leave it there and go away immediately.</i>

338
00:19:45,417 --> 00:19:46,552
Fine. Fine.

339
00:19:47,319 --> 00:19:48,520
He's a tough customer.

340
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:54,726
Okay, we've left it outside the shutter.

341
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:22,487
Now!

342
00:20:38,604 --> 00:20:39,605
Dr. Hachisuka!

343
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:42,474
- Dr. Hachisuka!
- Hey!

344
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:44,343
Hey, Dr. Hachisuka! Come out!

345
00:20:44,409 --> 00:20:45,911
We won't abandon you!

346
00:20:45,978 --> 00:20:48,046
We'll cure you with surgery!

347
00:20:48,113 --> 00:20:50,082
It will be Michiko Daimon
operating though!

348
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:56,054
Dr. Kaji and I will take over
caring for the infected patient!

349
00:20:56,121 --> 00:20:57,889
So quit worrying and get surgery!

350
00:20:57,956 --> 00:20:59,958
I've opened an OR for your sake!

351
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:01,660
No, thank you.

352
00:21:01,727 --> 00:21:02,861
How come?

353
00:21:03,462 --> 00:21:04,396
For the patient's sake?

354
00:21:04,997 --> 00:21:05,831
Hey!

355
00:21:05,897 --> 00:21:08,967
You're sick too! Don't try to show off!

356
00:21:09,034 --> 00:21:10,435
Just come out, would you?

357
00:21:10,502 --> 00:21:12,304
- Come out!
- Get out of there!

358
00:21:12,904 --> 00:21:14,039
You've got it wrong!

359
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,574
What do you mean?

360
00:21:16,875 --> 00:21:18,377
There is no patient.

361
00:21:19,311 --> 00:21:20,245
Are you nuts?

362
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:24,483
The only infected person is…

363
00:21:28,320 --> 00:21:29,588
me!

364
00:21:32,858 --> 00:21:37,062
I have been infected by the new virus.

365
00:21:39,498 --> 00:21:40,632
What?

366
00:21:40,699 --> 00:21:42,601
I cannot allow…

367
00:21:43,368 --> 00:21:45,337
anyone else to become infected!

368
00:21:49,508 --> 00:21:50,375
Sorry.

369
00:21:52,744 --> 00:21:56,081
We'll leave food and water
outside the shutter.

370
00:21:58,483 --> 00:21:59,651
Sorry.

371
00:22:04,323 --> 00:22:06,325
Michiko Daimon will do the surgery!

372
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:11,596
- The exit is this way!
- Not that way! This way!

373
00:22:26,211 --> 00:22:27,212
Dr. Daimon.

374
00:22:30,949 --> 00:22:33,251
So, you are infected.

375
00:22:34,219 --> 00:22:35,520
That's what I thought.

376
00:22:36,822 --> 00:22:38,623
You really are something, Dr. Daimon.

377
00:22:40,659 --> 00:22:41,727
Are you okay?

378
00:22:43,428 --> 00:22:46,398
Sorry, but I don't have time.

379
00:22:46,465 --> 00:22:47,666
Hold on!

380
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:55,040
What are you doing?

381
00:22:56,508 --> 00:23:00,779
I want to get as much information
about this new virus…

382
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:04,549
from my body as possible
before it's too late.

383
00:23:07,352 --> 00:23:09,688
You really are an infection maniac.

384
00:23:15,660 --> 00:23:19,364
I have a favor to ask you, Dr. Daimon.

385
00:23:20,365 --> 00:23:21,366
What?

386
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,736
When I die,

387
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:31,343
send this data to the research center
in Safiristan Kingdom.

388
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:36,081
I want it to assist
with developing medication.

389
00:23:36,148 --> 00:23:37,682
Quit talking about dying!

390
00:23:40,685 --> 00:23:44,956
If my death brings about a new drug…

391
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:47,359
it will save…

392
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:52,731
hundreds of millions,
if not billions of people.

393
00:23:57,536 --> 00:23:59,137
That is the deepest desire…

394
00:24:01,139 --> 00:24:02,541
of this infection maniac.

395
00:24:22,093 --> 00:24:23,295
Don't give up!

396
00:24:27,999 --> 00:24:28,900
I…

397
00:24:31,436 --> 00:24:34,039
I can only save
the patient I'm working on.

398
00:24:35,574 --> 00:24:36,875
But if I can save you…

399
00:24:38,610 --> 00:24:42,814
it will save the hundreds of millions
and billions you will save.

400
00:24:45,851 --> 00:24:46,918
So…

401
00:24:48,887 --> 00:24:49,955
don't give up.

402
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:03,535
I won't give up either.

403
00:25:08,206 --> 00:25:10,342
I'll make this a 100% perfect surgery!

404
00:25:19,885 --> 00:25:21,219
Thank you.

405
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:27,759
It is a terrible pity that I cannot…

406
00:25:29,661 --> 00:25:31,196
be operated on by you.

407
00:25:36,334 --> 00:25:37,969
I wanted to go with you again…

408
00:25:40,171 --> 00:25:42,107
to that sushi shop.

409
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:57,589
Hacchi!

410
00:25:59,824 --> 00:26:00,926
Hacchi!

411
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:18,710
Hacchi!

412
00:26:19,277 --> 00:26:20,145
Hacchi!

413
00:26:20,645 --> 00:26:21,580
Hacchi!

414
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,181
Hacchi!

415
00:26:24,349 --> 00:26:26,051
ANTI-SARS-COV

416
00:26:26,117 --> 00:26:26,952
Hacchi!

417
00:26:29,120 --> 00:26:30,989
INFECTION RESEARCH CENTER
OPENING CEREMONY

418
00:26:55,513 --> 00:26:58,850
I'll be using the antibody you developed.

419
00:27:07,559 --> 00:27:09,427
I won't let you do it alone this time!

420
00:27:10,662 --> 00:27:13,365
Give me that antibody too.

421
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:28,713
BP 125 over 83, pulse 88, normal sinus.

422
00:27:30,315 --> 00:27:32,517
We will now commence the removal

423
00:27:32,584 --> 00:27:35,387
of Ryutaro Hachisuka's left upper
quadrant organs.

424
00:27:35,954 --> 00:27:36,888
Here goes.

425
00:27:49,034 --> 00:27:49,901
<i>At this time in Japan,</i>

426
00:27:50,468 --> 00:27:52,370
there is only one infected person

427
00:27:52,937 --> 00:27:55,106
who is currently quarantining
in Totei University's

428
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:57,008
Infection Research Center.

429
00:27:57,075 --> 00:27:58,443
- Dr. Hiruma.
- Yes?

430
00:27:59,044 --> 00:28:00,145
How did this happen?

431
00:28:00,211 --> 00:28:02,881
I am terribly sorry.

432
00:28:02,947 --> 00:28:04,916
If infections spread,

433
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:08,153
this will cause
even greater turmoil than COVID.

434
00:28:08,219 --> 00:28:09,888
The citizens will fall into a panic!

435
00:28:09,954 --> 00:28:12,857
- That's right!
- It will spread, right?

436
00:28:12,924 --> 00:28:13,858
Excuse me!

437
00:28:14,426 --> 00:28:18,129
Doctors of the special council
and Governor Minami,

438
00:28:18,997 --> 00:28:22,100
there is no need for you to worry.

439
00:28:22,167 --> 00:28:25,003
We at Totei University Hospital

440
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:29,574
will completely prevent
this infectious disease from spreading.

441
00:28:30,141 --> 00:28:33,445
If I may say so myself,
I am the last line of defense,

442
00:28:33,511 --> 00:28:36,981
so leave it to me. Shigekatsu Hiruma.

443
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:38,750
I appreciate your cooperation.

444
00:28:38,817 --> 00:28:41,319
- You won't be sorry.
- Excuse me.

445
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:43,955
There's big trouble.

446
00:28:44,022 --> 00:28:46,758
The infected patient is Chief Hachisuka.

447
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:49,761
What's more, Dr. Daimon took over an OR

448
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:51,529
and is operating on him.

449
00:28:52,397 --> 00:28:55,266
Surely, you're kidding!

450
00:28:55,834 --> 00:28:58,570
"Surely, you're kidding"?

451
00:29:06,611 --> 00:29:08,179
Set the monopolar at 20-20.

452
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:13,118
It's ready.

453
00:29:15,854 --> 00:29:19,424
<i>Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>end this surgery immediately!</i>

454
00:29:19,491 --> 00:29:21,926
I knew you would call.

455
00:29:21,993 --> 00:29:23,995
<i>Dr. Daimon! Dr. Jonouchi!</i>

456
00:29:24,062 --> 00:29:25,630
End this surgery!

457
00:29:25,697 --> 00:29:29,234
Don't you care if you're infected
with that new virus?

458
00:29:30,235 --> 00:29:31,369
Would you shut up?

459
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:32,570
<i>What did you say?</i>

460
00:29:34,372 --> 00:29:36,341
Drag those two out of the OR.

461
00:29:36,941 --> 00:29:37,776
Yes, sir.

462
00:29:38,343 --> 00:29:41,412
Dr. Korogi, end that surgery by force!

463
00:29:41,479 --> 00:29:42,313
<i>What?</i>

464
00:29:42,380 --> 00:29:44,315
<i>But I'll get infected too.</i>

465
00:29:44,382 --> 00:29:45,850
Damn you, you idiot!

466
00:29:47,585 --> 00:29:48,586
PR Chief Mikuni,

467
00:29:48,653 --> 00:29:49,888
do something about this!

468
00:29:51,389 --> 00:29:52,290
She's ignoring us?

469
00:29:52,357 --> 00:29:54,559
Hey! Get Dr. Ebina!

470
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:56,060
Dr. Ebina isn't here.

471
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:57,695
Not since this morning.

472
00:29:57,762 --> 00:29:59,464
What about Dr. Hara and Dr. Kaji?

473
00:30:00,031 --> 00:30:00,899
<i>They're not here!</i>

474
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:02,066
Damn them!

475
00:30:14,212 --> 00:30:17,115
MASAKO OHMA, NURSE

476
00:30:31,529 --> 00:30:33,298
Dr. Daimon, stop!

477
00:30:33,364 --> 00:30:34,365
Get out.

478
00:30:34,432 --> 00:30:35,967
Don't show off on your own.

479
00:30:36,034 --> 00:30:37,302
Let us show off too!

480
00:30:37,368 --> 00:30:38,570
I said get out!

481
00:30:38,636 --> 00:30:40,104
We didn't come to stop you.

482
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:41,172
We came to help!

483
00:30:42,006 --> 00:30:42,841
All of you?

484
00:30:43,408 --> 00:30:45,543
We've all gotten injections
of the antibody

485
00:30:45,610 --> 00:30:46,911
that Dr. Hachisuka is developing.

486
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:52,283
- We won't run away this time.
- We have our pride as surgeons.

487
00:30:52,884 --> 00:30:54,452
I will stick with you too!

488
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:58,323
Then don't stand there! Hurry!

489
00:30:58,389 --> 00:30:59,624
- Right!
- Got it!

490
00:31:13,071 --> 00:31:16,274
With all these people operating,

491
00:31:17,108 --> 00:31:20,511
it will surely cause an outbreak!

492
00:31:20,578 --> 00:31:21,479
Yes, sir.

493
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:23,548
And that will be the end of…

494
00:31:24,148 --> 00:31:24,983
Governor…

495
00:31:26,618 --> 00:31:28,586
You couldn't prevent the spread?

496
00:31:28,653 --> 00:31:30,288
Well…

497
00:31:30,355 --> 00:31:31,956
What about the citizens?

498
00:31:32,490 --> 00:31:34,292
To protect the citizens' lives,

499
00:31:34,893 --> 00:31:36,861
we'll have to exercise force.

500
00:31:37,795 --> 00:31:40,164
Have the Ministry of Defense
mobilized the Self-Defense Forces

501
00:31:40,231 --> 00:31:42,734
and seal off
the Infection Research Center.

502
00:31:43,301 --> 00:31:45,904
Mobilize the SDF?

503
00:31:47,839 --> 00:31:49,974
SURGERY BRANCH

504
00:31:51,009 --> 00:31:52,010
Oh, dear.

505
00:31:52,076 --> 00:31:53,411
They're still at it.

506
00:31:53,478 --> 00:31:54,812
They're still at it!

507
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:57,248
Oh…

508
00:31:57,315 --> 00:32:00,451
Later today is the signing
for rebuilding the branch hospital.

509
00:32:01,019 --> 00:32:03,655
It's more important
that we stop this surgery.

510
00:32:03,721 --> 00:32:05,490
- Yes?
- Acting Director Hiruma.

511
00:32:06,157 --> 00:32:08,293
Your wife is being released today.

512
00:32:08,359 --> 00:32:09,360
Is that right?

513
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,363
- Dear.
- Yes?

514
00:32:12,964 --> 00:32:16,467
- It's been a while.
- Yes, it has. Hi.

515
00:32:16,534 --> 00:32:17,568
Oh, dear.

516
00:32:17,635 --> 00:32:18,770
Stop this!

517
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:25,009
Gastric cardia resection. Linear stapler.

518
00:32:25,076 --> 00:32:25,944
Here.

519
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:33,618
- Kelly clamp.
- Here.

520
00:32:49,167 --> 00:32:50,835
This is completely out of hand.

521
00:32:51,736 --> 00:32:54,038
They've resigned themselves
to being infected.

522
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:57,041
It's so terribly reckless.

523
00:32:58,743 --> 00:33:01,980
None of them can avoid being infected.

524
00:33:07,919 --> 00:33:10,521
Dr. Korogi, are you going somewhere?

525
00:33:10,588 --> 00:33:11,723
I'm going back to New York.

526
00:33:11,789 --> 00:33:12,824
It's too dangerous here.

527
00:33:14,058 --> 00:33:15,693
Don't end up like them.

528
00:33:16,294 --> 00:33:19,163
If you know how risky something is
but you don't avoid it,

529
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:20,865
you're just stupid.

530
00:33:23,401 --> 00:33:24,235
I…

531
00:33:26,070 --> 00:33:29,440
I am proud to have them as my seniors!

532
00:33:32,076 --> 00:33:32,910
Me too.

533
00:33:33,511 --> 00:33:35,046
I want to be a surgeon like them.

534
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:37,782
- Me too.
- Me too!

535
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:38,950
- Me too.
- Me too.

536
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:50,962
Suit yourselves!

537
00:34:03,307 --> 00:34:04,308
Dr. Kuwagata,

538
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:05,943
do something to stop them!

539
00:34:06,010 --> 00:34:07,011
Stop them!

540
00:34:07,612 --> 00:34:09,614
We must go.
The contract signing will start.

541
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:13,217
What contract is that?

542
00:34:17,488 --> 00:34:18,589
Dear…

543
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:23,127
What are you scheming now?

544
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:27,799
If you call yourself a doctor,

545
00:34:28,933 --> 00:34:30,701
then instead of doing those things,

546
00:34:32,203 --> 00:34:34,705
why don't you save a precious life!

547
00:34:52,623 --> 00:34:54,158
BP 70!

548
00:34:54,225 --> 00:34:55,426
Pulse 110, he's arrhythmic!

549
00:34:55,493 --> 00:34:57,028
Continuous PVCs.

550
00:34:57,095 --> 00:34:59,931
R-on-T as well. Circulation unstable!

551
00:34:59,997 --> 00:35:02,100
The virus may be causing pericarditis.

552
00:35:02,166 --> 00:35:03,668
This is bad, Dr. Daimon!

553
00:35:03,734 --> 00:35:05,136
Injecting amiodarone.

554
00:35:05,203 --> 00:35:06,804
Got it. I'm counting on you.

555
00:35:06,871 --> 00:35:08,439
I'll do the portal vein and gallbladder.

556
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:09,774
- Pean.
- Here.

557
00:35:09,841 --> 00:35:11,742
It's not even half-finished.
Will it be okay?

558
00:35:11,809 --> 00:35:13,177
- Hurry up!
- Right.

559
00:35:48,112 --> 00:35:51,015
What? I thought you ran away to New York.

560
00:35:56,621 --> 00:35:58,990
I'll remove the retroperitoneum
and left kidney.

561
00:35:59,056 --> 00:36:00,358
Energy device.

562
00:36:00,424 --> 00:36:01,359
Oh… Here!

563
00:36:26,284 --> 00:36:28,319
Left kidney and retroperitoneum
removal complete.

564
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,188
That was fast!

565
00:36:30,254 --> 00:36:31,656
You're amazing, White Jack.

566
00:36:31,722 --> 00:36:33,591
You really weren't a fraud. Sorry.

567
00:36:41,599 --> 00:36:43,234
BP back to 90.

568
00:36:43,301 --> 00:36:44,602
Circulation normal again.

569
00:36:45,970 --> 00:36:48,172
Let's remove the tumor next.

570
00:36:48,239 --> 00:36:49,574
- Metz.
- Here.

571
00:36:49,640 --> 00:36:50,708
- DeBakey.
- Here.

572
00:36:52,577 --> 00:36:53,978
- Get me a DeBakey too.
- Here.

573
00:37:04,789 --> 00:37:07,391
Acting Director Hiruma,
the signing will start!

574
00:37:08,526 --> 00:37:09,360
Forget that!

575
00:37:09,427 --> 00:37:10,261
Keep quiet.

576
00:37:18,703 --> 00:37:19,670
You can do it,

577
00:37:19,737 --> 00:37:20,905
Dr. Daimon.

578
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:24,075
Don't you die…

579
00:37:25,643 --> 00:37:27,178
Ryutaro Hachisuka.

580
00:37:38,122 --> 00:37:41,025
ANESTHETIZED TIME, SURGERY TIME

581
00:37:47,665 --> 00:37:51,569
The tumor has thoroughly infiltrated
the ventral aorta.

582
00:37:53,871 --> 00:37:56,040
We'll remove the aorta with the tumor

583
00:37:56,107 --> 00:37:58,042
and reconstruct
the superior mesenteric artery.

584
00:37:58,109 --> 00:37:59,343
We'll need a vascular graft.

585
00:37:59,410 --> 00:38:00,811
Got it.

586
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:05,049
Clamping the ventral aorta. Fogarty clamp.

587
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:06,050
Here.

588
00:38:16,927 --> 00:38:17,928
- Cooper.
- Here.

589
00:38:26,537 --> 00:38:27,905
Cardiac arrest!

590
00:38:28,606 --> 00:38:29,707
Why?

591
00:39:14,752 --> 00:39:15,753
Hacchi!

592
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:17,555
Come back!

593
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:20,291
Come back!

594
00:39:46,751 --> 00:39:48,753
Hey. What are you doing, Demon?

595
00:39:53,591 --> 00:39:54,492
Scalpel.

596
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,260
Right.

597
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,230
Here.

598
00:40:14,311 --> 00:40:16,113
Opening the pericardial sac.
Number 11 scalpel.

599
00:40:16,180 --> 00:40:17,047
Here.

600
00:40:24,054 --> 00:40:25,089
- Metz.
- Here.

601
00:40:50,915 --> 00:40:51,882
I will…

602
00:40:53,717 --> 00:40:55,186
not fail.

603
00:41:50,307 --> 00:41:51,575
Pulse has returned!

604
00:41:51,642 --> 00:41:52,710
Injecting atropine.

605
00:41:54,278 --> 00:41:55,346
Let's continue the surgery.

606
00:41:55,412 --> 00:41:57,014
- 3-0 monofilament.
- Here.

607
00:42:36,520 --> 00:42:37,821
<i>Michiko…</i>

608
00:42:51,368 --> 00:42:52,836
Dr. Daimon…

609
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:25,970
Okay, see you later, Shigekatsu.

610
00:43:26,637 --> 00:43:28,505
You submit this.

611
00:43:30,708 --> 00:43:31,842
Hana.

612
00:43:33,744 --> 00:43:34,945
You're really leaving?

613
00:43:35,012 --> 00:43:39,183
You can climb the career ladder
all you want without me around.

614
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:46,757
Who is it?

615
00:43:50,294 --> 00:43:51,629
She's leaving me…

616
00:43:54,798 --> 00:43:56,367
Greetings!

617
00:43:56,433 --> 00:44:01,839
Congratulations on your
and Chief Hachisuka's surgeries!

618
00:44:02,740 --> 00:44:05,042
I'm terribly sorry

619
00:44:05,109 --> 00:44:09,013
for visiting you in your home
while you're so busy.

620
00:44:09,079 --> 00:44:10,314
This is a melon.

621
00:44:13,984 --> 00:44:15,419
This is the bill.

622
00:44:21,625 --> 00:44:24,328
BILL FOR HANAKO HIRUMA'S SURGERY.

623
00:44:24,395 --> 00:44:26,830
Oh, dear! I had always heard
she was expensive,

624
00:44:26,897 --> 00:44:28,599
but she really is!

625
00:44:29,433 --> 00:44:31,635
Can you please give a discount?

626
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:34,338
No.

627
00:44:35,205 --> 00:44:37,541
I will pay the price you've asked for.

628
00:44:38,275 --> 00:44:39,209
Yes, sir!

629
00:44:40,611 --> 00:44:46,316
Thank you so much for saving Hana.

630
00:44:49,053 --> 00:44:53,323
I am truly grateful.

631
00:44:53,390 --> 00:44:55,626
Thank you!

632
00:44:55,693 --> 00:44:57,361
Darling…

633
00:44:58,262 --> 00:45:01,231
If you hadn't scolded me that day,

634
00:45:01,832 --> 00:45:02,966
right now,

635
00:45:03,834 --> 00:45:05,002
I would be…

636
00:45:06,170 --> 00:45:09,573
<i>The police have arrested</i>
<i>two individuals on suspicion</i>

637
00:45:09,640 --> 00:45:12,576
<i>of corruption in the Totei University</i>
<i>Hospital rebuilding contract.</i>

638
00:45:12,643 --> 00:45:15,546
<i>I didn't do it! This is ridiculous!</i>

639
00:45:15,612 --> 00:45:17,347
<i>47-year-old…</i>

640
00:45:17,414 --> 00:45:19,883
Thank goodness.

641
00:45:20,584 --> 00:45:21,652
Then

642
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:24,688
can you pay for this as well?

643
00:45:25,189 --> 00:45:28,726
BILL FOR RYUTARO HACHISUKA'S SURGERY

644
00:45:28,792 --> 00:45:29,793
Dr. Hachisuka's surgery?

645
00:45:30,527 --> 00:45:32,129
This doesn't involve me!

646
00:45:32,196 --> 00:45:33,931
Don't talk like that.

647
00:45:33,997 --> 00:45:35,566
We'll pay!

648
00:45:35,632 --> 00:45:37,034
Hana…

649
00:45:37,101 --> 00:45:38,469
- We'll sell this place.
- What?

650
00:45:38,535 --> 00:45:40,704
- We'll sell the villa in Karuizawa!
- What?

651
00:45:40,771 --> 00:45:43,440
- We'll sell these too!
- What?

652
00:45:44,174 --> 00:45:46,543
And we'll pay for everything!

653
00:45:47,978 --> 00:45:49,580
Shigekatsu Hiruma,

654
00:45:50,781 --> 00:45:52,616
his troubles are solved.

655
00:45:54,952 --> 00:46:00,924
I made a truckload of money!

656
00:46:00,991 --> 00:46:02,926
We're in the money!

657
00:46:02,993 --> 00:46:05,229
We're in the money!

658
00:46:06,797 --> 00:46:10,267
This feels totally fantastic!

659
00:46:10,334 --> 00:46:14,071
My first bath in two weeks!

660
00:46:14,138 --> 00:46:16,206
A bath after quarantining is awesome!

661
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:21,411
- It's the greatest!
- It's the greatest!

662
00:46:21,478 --> 00:46:23,046
Shut up!

663
00:46:23,113 --> 00:46:25,749
Thank goodness nobody caught it.

664
00:46:25,816 --> 00:46:28,185
That new virus can't defeat us.

665
00:46:28,252 --> 00:46:29,686
Change and challenge!

666
00:46:29,753 --> 00:46:33,157
Japanese public baths are amazing!

667
00:46:33,223 --> 00:46:34,691
You're amazing, White Jack.

668
00:46:34,758 --> 00:46:36,026
But you're Japanese, right?

669
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:37,995
Don't use English!

670
00:46:38,061 --> 00:46:41,932
- This feels totally awesome!
- This feels totally awesome!

671
00:46:41,999 --> 00:46:44,001
The post-op results are very good.

672
00:46:44,601 --> 00:46:47,604
But keep careful records
of your daily calorie intake

673
00:46:47,671 --> 00:46:49,273
and your liquid input and output.

674
00:46:50,073 --> 00:46:52,309
Yes, ma'am. I will.

675
00:46:54,812 --> 00:46:56,780
The Infection Research Center…

676
00:46:57,848 --> 00:46:59,550
has been shut down.

677
00:47:00,417 --> 00:47:01,251
It has?

678
00:47:01,852 --> 00:47:04,988
But your antibody worked.

679
00:47:06,423 --> 00:47:07,658
Fortunately,

680
00:47:07,724 --> 00:47:10,227
there was no outbreak.

681
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:14,731
But I can't get any more grants
or donations.

682
00:47:16,233 --> 00:47:17,134
I see.

683
00:47:17,201 --> 00:47:18,335
Tomorrow…

684
00:47:21,104 --> 00:47:23,807
I will be traveling
to the Safiristan Kingdom.

685
00:47:24,575 --> 00:47:25,409
What?

686
00:47:26,810 --> 00:47:31,882
I will deliver the data on the new virus
to Dr. Shelp…

687
00:47:33,483 --> 00:47:35,853
and visit the countries of Africa.

688
00:47:37,187 --> 00:47:38,822
I see.

689
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:42,092
With the life you saved…

690
00:47:44,361 --> 00:47:48,265
I want to save the hundreds of millions
of people suffering from…

691
00:47:48,899 --> 00:47:49,933
infectious diseases.

692
00:47:59,142 --> 00:48:00,210
Would you like…

693
00:48:02,246 --> 00:48:03,080
to…

694
00:48:03,146 --> 00:48:03,981
to…

695
00:48:04,047 --> 00:48:05,682
to join me?

696
00:48:07,184 --> 00:48:08,285
Well…

697
00:48:08,352 --> 00:48:09,853
I was thinking,

698
00:48:09,920 --> 00:48:12,189
an infection maniac and a surgery maniac

699
00:48:12,256 --> 00:48:15,125
would make the perfect partners.

700
00:48:15,192 --> 00:48:16,093
Jeez.

701
00:48:16,159 --> 00:48:17,060
Well…

702
00:48:17,127 --> 00:48:18,028
I mean…

703
00:48:18,095 --> 00:48:19,029
I want

704
00:48:19,096 --> 00:48:21,431
to have lots of octopus with you!

705
00:48:23,166 --> 00:48:25,636
I would love to eat octopus!

706
00:48:27,371 --> 00:48:28,906
Near the Safiristan Kingdom

707
00:48:29,506 --> 00:48:30,807
is Mauritania,

708
00:48:30,874 --> 00:48:32,142
a source of octopus!

709
00:48:32,209 --> 00:48:33,110
Really?

710
00:48:35,178 --> 00:48:36,146
Please…

711
00:48:37,648 --> 00:48:38,982
have octopus with me!

712
00:48:46,823 --> 00:48:48,959
Michiko sure is late.

713
00:48:49,026 --> 00:48:51,361
Where in the world did she go? Right?

714
00:48:51,428 --> 00:48:52,963
Is she on a date?

715
00:48:53,030 --> 00:48:55,265
Don't be ridiculous. Not Michiko.

716
00:48:55,332 --> 00:48:57,034
You can't know that!

717
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:58,835
You can't know that, right?

718
00:48:59,403 --> 00:49:01,605
BEN CASEY, GANNON

719
00:49:03,740 --> 00:49:04,574
Hey!

720
00:49:05,208 --> 00:49:06,109
Oh, wow!

721
00:49:06,176 --> 00:49:07,244
Akira!

722
00:49:07,311 --> 00:49:09,446
You've hidden stacks of bills here!

723
00:49:09,513 --> 00:49:11,481
- Stacks of bills?
- Look!

724
00:49:11,548 --> 00:49:12,883
There's a ton!

725
00:49:16,353 --> 00:49:18,288
I've kept this secret until now,

726
00:49:18,355 --> 00:49:21,058
but I've been saving up
a lot of the surgery fees.

727
00:49:21,625 --> 00:49:22,893
- I knew it!
- I knew it!

728
00:49:22,960 --> 00:49:24,428
To tell the truth,

729
00:49:24,494 --> 00:49:27,130
I was saving it all

730
00:49:27,197 --> 00:49:31,835
to build a hospital overseas
where Michiko can operate all she wants.

731
00:49:32,769 --> 00:49:34,738
What an amazing hospital!

732
00:49:34,805 --> 00:49:36,540
That place looks awesome!

733
00:49:36,606 --> 00:49:38,909
That's right. But you know what?

734
00:49:40,143 --> 00:49:43,547
I still don't have
nearly enough to pay for it.

735
00:49:43,613 --> 00:49:47,117
- So instead, I got this.
- Yes, I guess this isn't enough.

736
00:49:47,184 --> 00:49:49,686
It's a Michiko-roid!

737
00:49:51,688 --> 00:49:52,789
Behold!

738
00:50:01,298 --> 00:50:03,233
Ms. Daimon!

739
00:50:08,972 --> 00:50:11,875
What? It's walking toward us!

740
00:50:13,577 --> 00:50:14,511
MICHIKO-ROID

741
00:50:15,479 --> 00:50:16,813
It stopped!

742
00:50:17,881 --> 00:50:19,416
It's cold!

743
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:22,853
No way! It smiled!

744
00:50:22,919 --> 00:50:26,256
This way, no matter how virulent
a virus we're faced with,

745
00:50:26,323 --> 00:50:27,657
we'll be safe and secure.

746
00:50:28,258 --> 00:50:32,229
And with 100 of these,
we can save 100 times more patients.

747
00:50:40,871 --> 00:50:42,606
<i>- Ron!</i>
- What?

748
00:50:43,540 --> 00:50:44,374
Akira,

749
00:50:44,975 --> 00:50:48,245
I am terribly sorry.

750
00:50:53,984 --> 00:50:55,719
Thirteen orphans.

751
00:50:57,187 --> 00:51:02,426
Thank you very much
for allowing me to win.

752
00:51:02,492 --> 00:51:03,827
How aggravating!

753
00:51:03,894 --> 00:51:06,196
She's so polite!

754
00:51:06,263 --> 00:51:07,631
This droid is good!

755
00:51:07,697 --> 00:51:08,865
Let's play again.

756
00:51:09,833 --> 00:51:11,101
I will.

757
00:51:11,701 --> 00:51:13,603
Let me win next time.

758
00:51:14,104 --> 00:51:15,439
I won't.

759
00:51:18,842 --> 00:51:20,877
INTERNATIONAL FLIGHTS

760
00:51:24,881 --> 00:51:26,416
BOARDING PASS

761
00:51:26,483 --> 00:51:28,118
MICHIKO DAIMON, RYUTARO HACHISUKA

762
00:52:06,323 --> 00:52:08,892
<i>Flight 815 at 3:30 p.m. for Safiristan</i>

763
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:12,696
<i>will be departing momentarily.</i>

764
00:52:12,762 --> 00:52:16,700
<i>Passengers on flight 815 for Safiristan</i>

765
00:52:16,766 --> 00:52:18,635
<i>are requested to board at gate 9.</i>

766
00:52:18,702 --> 00:52:21,238
<i>Please do not be late.</i>

767
00:52:34,417 --> 00:52:37,654
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

768
00:52:37,721 --> 00:52:39,523
He sure is late.

769
00:52:41,324 --> 00:52:44,060
Why isn't that damn Hacchi here?

770
00:52:45,295 --> 00:52:47,164
- You're waiting for Dr. Hachisuka?
- Yes.

771
00:52:47,731 --> 00:52:50,767
Dr. Hachisuka left on a flight
for Africa this afternoon.

772
00:52:50,834 --> 00:52:51,835
What?

773
00:52:52,836 --> 00:52:58,542
But he said, "Have… Have octopus with me!"

774
00:53:00,277 --> 00:53:01,278
Didn't he mean sushi?

775
00:53:02,379 --> 00:53:07,083
I heard from Dr. Hachisuka
that you're a genius surgeon.

776
00:53:07,951 --> 00:53:09,286
But you're a ditz, huh?

777
00:53:09,853 --> 00:53:11,521
I am not.

778
00:53:11,588 --> 00:53:13,590
Oh, sorry about that.

779
00:53:13,657 --> 00:53:15,525
I'm starving!

780
00:53:16,526 --> 00:53:17,694
Shall I serve you something?

781
00:53:17,761 --> 00:53:18,595
Yes!

782
00:53:19,596 --> 00:53:23,600
I'll have octopus, <i>kohada,</i> and squid legs,

783
00:53:23,667 --> 00:53:27,103
plus fatty tuna, urchin, roe,
sea bream, abalone, and…

784
00:53:28,638 --> 00:53:29,639
Sir?

785
00:53:32,375 --> 00:53:33,677
Are you okay?

786
00:53:33,743 --> 00:53:34,744
<i>She hates groups,</i>

787
00:53:34,811 --> 00:53:36,079
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

788
00:53:36,146 --> 00:53:37,547
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

789
00:53:38,148 --> 00:53:41,451
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

790
00:53:41,518 --> 00:53:42,852
<i>to work her way up.</i>

791
00:53:47,490 --> 00:53:49,559
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

792
00:53:51,228 --> 00:53:54,598
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

793
00:53:54,664 --> 00:53:56,066
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
